<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson posts 33 pct rise in '96 profit.</title>
<headline>Ericsson posts 33 pct rise in '96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group LM Ericsson AB reports for the 12 months ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			   10,152 vs   7,615</p>
<p> Turnover				  124,266 vs  98,780</p>
<p> Order bookings			  138,048 vs 104,981</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		7.27  vs    5.83</p>
<p> Proposed dividend per share (SKR)    2.50 vs    1.75</p>
<p> Other operating income		  1,193 vs     487</p>
<p> Associate interests			 424 vs     414</p>
<p> Turnover costs			   70,106 vs  54,323</p>
<p> Admin, sales costs		     40,803 vs  33,580</p>
<p> Depreciation				4,216 vs   3,614</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	10,758 vs   8,164</p>
<p> Net financial items			 412 vs	58</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 11,170 vs   8,222</p>
<p> Minorities				  1,018 vs     607</p>
<p> Tax					   3,042 vs   2,176</p>
<p> Net profit				  7,110 vs   5,439</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll of 18 analysts found the market expected Ericsson to post a pre-tax profit of 10.03 billion crowns for calendar 1996, sales 117.50 billion crowns, earnings per share were expected to rise to 6.95 crowns. The poll found an average forecast for a dividend of 2.05 crowns a share.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
